## Issues

- GitHub Issues are used to track problems, tasks and ideas.

- An issue could be:

    - Fix login bug
    - Add dark mode
    - Improve database performance
    - Add password reset
    - Write tests for authentication

- Issues are useful because I can keep track of work without relying on memory.

---

## Labels

- GitHub Issues can have labels.

- Example labels:

    bug
    feature
    documentation
    enhancement
    help wanted
    good first issue

- Labels make it easier to organise issues.

---

## Milestones

- Milestones group issues and Pull Requests around a larger goal.

- Example:

    Version 1.0

- Could contain:

    - User registration
    - Login
    - Password reset
    - User profiles
    - Testing

- This helps organise development.

